# Billing Renewal & Dunning (Permanent)

## Law

**Expire locks work; never deletes tenant data.**

| State | Writable | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `trial` / `active` | yes | Paid or trial period (`endsAt` in future) |
| `grace` | yes | Past `endsAt`, within `GRACE_DURATION_DAYS` — renew CTA |
| `expired` | no | Past grace — read-only; data retained |
| `pending_payment` | no | Never activated / unpaid Business #2+ |

## Clock rules

- Effective status must honor **grace** before **expired** (read-time + persisted job).
- Daily BullMQ job (`billing.dunning`) on **SAAS** only: persist `grace` / `expired`, send SMS reminders.
- SELF_HOSTED: skip subscription dunning (license path).

## Notifications

- Channels: **SMS** via `SmsSender` transactional API (same provider as OTP).
- Email: **non-goal** for this slice (document if adding later).
- Idempotent rows in `subscription_dunning_notices` keyed by `(subscriptionId, kind, periodKey)`.
- Kinds: `reminder_7d`, `reminder_1d`, `entered_grace`, `entered_expired`.
- Never log OTP/payment secrets in notice meta or SMS bodies beyond business name + status.

## Renewal

- User renews via existing SAAS checkout → `active` + new `endsAt`.
- No silent auto-charge / stored card retry in MVP.

## Forbidden

- Deleting Business/documents because subscription expired.
- Skipping grace by jumping straight to expired at read-time without the grace window.
- Running cross-tenant dunning SMS on SELF_HOSTED.
